    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0417" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/13803: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-23T17:00:00-04:00">August 23, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. A United Press despatch from London was received in this country on August 21
                    stating that the President “has approved whatever action Great Britain and
                    Russia deem necessary to purge Iran of Nazi influences.” It is further stated in
                    this despatch that the question of Iran was dealt with thoroughly at the
                    conference between the President and the British Prime Minister.<anchor n="85"
                        xml:id="d387-f1"/></p>
                <p>You should inform the Foreign Office without delay that the President has denied
                    the accuracy of the despatch above mentioned. The Secretary has informed the
                    Iranian Minister that the despatch is untrue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d387-f1" n="85" xml:id="d387-f1-content">
                <p>Known as the Atlantic Conference, August 9–12, 1941; see <ref
                        target="frus1941v01#pg_341">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp.
                        341</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
